e across devices.\\n- 08:04–08:06 UTC: User requested HTTPS upgrade and approved execution now. Decision: upgraded Ops Cockpit service to native HTTPS (TLS) mode using self-signed certificate on port 18888; service unit switched to HTTPS profile, certificate/key generated under `/etc/ssl/ops-cockpit`, permissions fixed for runtime access, service restarted healthy. Evidence: `ops-cockpit.service` active (running) with HTTPS profile; `curl -k https://127.0.0.1:18888/` returns HTTP 200 with auth. RAG: GREEN (HTTPS enabled), AMBER for trust UX because self-signed cert will show browser warning until domain CA cert is installed. Owners: Mạnh AI (TLS infra), Hà AI (runtime fixes), Huy AI (voice validation on secure context), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: browser certificate warning (self-signed). Next: if user provides domain, issue trusted TLS cert (Let’s Encrypt) to remove warning and finalize production-grade voice UX.\\n\"}]}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-5.3-codex","usage":{"input":132,"output":847,"cacheRead":163712,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":164691,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1776067589107,"responseId":""}}
