tiến độ bàn giao dashboard và các cải tiến UX/ngôn ngữ; duy trì AMBER cho các hạng mục cần quyết định từ người dùng (TLS/HTTPS internet exposure, chuẩn giá token để tính chi phí chính xác, dữ liệu bot hội thoại có cấu trúc để giảm fallback). Owners: MINH AI tổng hợp; Mạnh AI xử lý hạ tầng/TLS khi được duyệt; Huy AI tinh chỉnh UI; Hà AI chuẩn hóa dữ liệu & cost logic; Huyền AI chốt AC/UAT. ETA: 09:00 UTC cho vòng cập nhật kế tiếp. Blockers: thiếu quyết định chính thức về truy cập từ internet + bảng giá billing chuẩn. Next: chờ user phê duyệt và triển khai ngay trong giờ tới.\n- 07:59 UTC: User requested ChatGPT-like voice conversation with MINH AI. Decision: feasible but currently blocked by browser microphone security because dashboard is served over HTTP public IP (Web Speech/mic requires secure context HTTPS or localhost). Proposed delivery plan \"Voice Mode Lite\": push-to-talk STT + TTS playback + conversation transcript in dashboard after HTTPS is enabled. RAG: AMBER (clear path, one infra blocker). Owners: Mạnh AI (HTTPS/reverse proxy), Huy AI (voice UI controls), Hà AI (voice pipeline endpoint/session relay), Huyền AI (UAT scenarios). ETA: ~2 hours after approval + domain/HTTPS path confirmed. Blockers: no HTTPS endpoint/domain configured yet. Next: get user approval on HTTPS method (domain + TLS or Tailscale/localhost) then execute implementation sprint.\n- 08:02–08:04 UTC: User approved immediate delivery and requested ChatGPT-like conversation mode with Vietnamese female voice and polite address style. Decision: implemented Voice Mode Lite in dashboard now: (1) voice control panel, (2) browser speech recognition (`vi-VN`) push-to-talk, (3) MINH AI response endpoint `/api/minh-chat`, (4) TTS playback preferring Vietnamese female voice, (5) polite response persona in reply generator, (6) in-panel transcript log for turn-by-turn exchange. Evidence: HTML contains voice controls (`Bắt đầu hội thoại`, `Giữ để nói`), JS hooks for SpeechRecognition + TTS + askMinh flow, API call test returned polite Vietnamese response with formatted token/cost numbers. RAG: GREEN (core experience delivered), AMBER for browser/HTTPS dependency on microphone in some environments. Owners: Huy AI (voice UI), Hà AI (voice API + persona logic), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: microphone capture may fail on non-HTTPS context depending browser policy. Next: if user confirms domain, execute HTTPS enablement to stabilize voice capture across devices.\n- 08:04–08:06 UTC: User requested HTTPS upgrade and approved execution now. Decision: upgraded Ops Cockpit service to native HTTPS (TLS) mode using self-signed certificate on port 18888; service unit switched to HTTPS profile, certificate/key generated under `/etc/ssl/ops-cockpit`, permissions fixed for runtime access, service restarted healthy. Evidence: `ops-cockpit.service` active (running) with HTTPS profile; `curl -k https://127.0.0.1:18888/` returns HTTP 200 with auth. RAG: GREEN (HTTPS enabled), AMBER for trust UX because self-signed cert will show browser warning until domain CA cert is installed. Owners: Mạnh AI (TLS infra), Hà AI (runtime fixes), Huy AI (voice validation on secure context), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: browser certificate warning (self-signed). Next: if user provides domain, issue trusted TLS cert (Let’s Encrypt) to remove warning and finalize production-grade voice UX.\n- 08:08–08:11 UTC: User requested full text communication channel on dashboard (as alternative to Telegram) with image attach/capture and conversation continuity. Decision: implemented dashboard-native chat channel enhancements: (1) text chat endpoint `/api/minh-chat` returns dialogue history, (2) image upload endpoint `/api/upload-image` accepts base64 images and stores under local uploads, (3) UI buttons for `Đính kèm ảnh` and `Chụp ảnh` (camera via getUserMedia), (4) attachments passed into chat context for MINH AI response flow. Evidence: HTTPS POST `/api/upload-image` returns file URL; HTTPS POST `/api/minh-chat` with attachment returns polite Vietnamese acknowledgement and history payload. RAG: GREEN (channel capability delivered), AMBER for production-grade media governance (retention policy/size limits not yet enforced). Owners: Huy AI (chat+media UI), Hà AI (chat/upload APIs), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart HTTPS), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: no media retention/cleanup policy yet; camera permission depends on browser user consent. Next: add file-size limit + retention cleanup + optional image moderation/log policy.\n- 08:12–08:13 UTC: User reported web inaccessible after HTTPS migration. Verification evidence: service healthy (`ops-cockpit.service` active), port 18888 listening, local HTTPS responds (HTTP 200 with auth). Likely user-side access issue due protocol/cert flow (must use https + accept self-signed warning) or network path on custom port. Decision: provide immediate recovery instructions and propose mitigation path (move to trusted cert + standard 443). RAG: AMBER (service up, access friction exists). Owners: Mạnh AI investigate connectivity path, Huy AI provide user guidance UX banner, PM coordinate comms. ETA: immediate guidance now; 30–60m for 443/trusted-cert plan after user approval. Blockers: self-signed cert warning + possible custom-port reachability constraints. Next: confirm user can open explicit HTTPS URL; if still fail, execute migration to domain/443.\n- 08:00–08:02 UTC: Internal scrum sync executed via sessions_spawn with explicit agentId (manh/huy/ha/huyen) and evidence-based 4-field updates collected. Decision: giữ focus 1 giờ tới vào chuyển từ planning sang artifact thực thi (OpenAPI/event spec/ticket assignment/SIT unlock), không mở rộng scope mới. RAG: Overall AMBER (all owners responded with evidence, but implementation artifacts/tickets still missing). Owner updates & ETA: Mạnh AI—08:05–08:20 chốt OpenAPI v1, 08:20–08:40 event envelope + idempotency rule, 0