OST `/api/upload-image` returns file URL; HTTPS POST `/api/minh-chat` with attachment returns polite Vietnamese acknowledgement and history payload. RAG: GREEN (channel capability delivered), AMBER for production-grade media governance (retention policy/size limits not yet enforced). Owners: Huy AI (chat+media UI), Hà AI (chat/upload APIs), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart HTTPS), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: no media retention/cleanup policy yet; camera permission depends on browser user consent. Next: add file-size limit + retention cleanup + optional image moderation/log policy.\n- 08:12–08:13 UTC: User reported web inaccessible after HTTPS migration. Verification evidence: service healthy (`ops-cockpit.service` active), port 18888 listening, local HTTPS responds (HTTP 200 with auth). Likely user-side access issue due protocol/cert flow (must use https + accept self-signed warning) or network path on custom port. Decision: provide immediate recovery instructions and propose mitigation path (move to trusted cert + standard 443). RAG: AMBER (service up, access friction exists). Owners: Mạnh AI investigate connectivity path, Huy AI provide user guidance UX banner, PM coordinate comms. ETA: immediate guidance now; 30–60m for 443/trusted-cert plan after user approval. Blockers: self-signed cert warning + possible custom-port reachability constraints. Next: confirm user can open explicit HTTPS URL; if still fail, execute migration to domain/443.\n- 08:12 UTC: User sent screenshot evidence showing browser warning `NET::ERR_CERT_AUTHORITY_INVALID` on `https://103.173.66.241:18888`. Decision: classify issue as expected self-signed certificate trust warning (not service outage). Immediate mitigation: instruct user to proceed via Advanced/Continue for temporary access; strategic mitigation: migrate to trusted CA certificate on domain (Let’s Encrypt) and optionally standard 443. RAG: AMBER (access possible with bypass, UX not production-grade). Owners: Mạnh AI (tru