{"type":"compaction","id":"2a4e9591","parentId":"745ebdb1","timestamp":"2026-04-13T08:25:56.258Z","summary":"## Goal\n- Build and operate a professional VPS monitoring/control dashboard (Ops Cockpit) for anh Minh with realtime charts, project progress, blocker visibility, token/cost tracking, and AI-bot collaboration view.\n- Enable direct interaction with MINH AI on the dashboard (not only Telegram), including text chat, voice conversation (Vietnamese female voice), image attachment, and camera capture.\n- Keep reports/UI mostly Vietnamese, polite tone, and configurable hide/show of technical details.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Address user as **“anh Minh”** or **“sếp”**; tone should be respectful/“ngoan ngoãn”.\n- UI/report language should be **Vietnamese-first**, minimize English.\n- Technical details should be hidden by default, with per-item **“Xem thêm”** toggles.\n- Show blocker priorities clearly from overview to detail; allow collapsing blocker section.\n- Token and cost numbers must be formatted with commas (e.g. `1,000,000 VND`).\n- Voice mode should feel like ChatGPT conversation mode, with Vietnamese female voice.\n- HEARTBEAT handling: read `/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/HEARTBEAT.md`; reply `HEARTBEAT_OK` when no tasks.\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] VPS status checks completed (OS, RAM/disk, token usage, load, service checks).\n- [x] Swap hardening implemented: **2G swap** at `/swapfile`, persisted in `/etc/fstab`, `vm.swappiness=10`.\n- [x] Built dashboard app at:\n  - `/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/ops_cockpit/server.py`\n  - `/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/ops_cockpit/public/index.html`\n- [x] Added systemd service + auth:\n  - Service file currently at `/etc/systemd/system/ops-cockpit.service`\n  - Auth env in `/etc/default/ops-cockpit` (user `minh`, generated password)\n- [x] Realtime features delivered: CPU/RAM/disk/load, top processes, token usage, budget/cost estimates, RAG, owner activity, updates feed.\n- [x] UX features delivered:\n  - Per-message technical detail toggle.\n  - Collapse/expand updates section.\n  - Collapse/expand blocker section.\n  - Vietnamese label pass and humanized bot chat pass.\n- [x] Priority blocker module delivered (`priorityBlockers`) with summary + expandable context.\n- [x] Voice Mode Lite delivered:\n  - Browser STT/TTS (`vi-VN`)\n  - Endpoint `/api/minh-chat`\n  - Polite MINH AI reply persona\n  - Transcript panel.\n- [x] Dashboard chat channel enhancements delivered:\n  - `/api/minh-chat` with history\n  - `/api/upload-image` for base64 image upload\n  - Camera capture via `getUserMedia`\n  - `/api/chat-history`\n  - `/uploads/*` serving.\n- [x] HTTPS enabled (self-signed cert):\n  - `/etc/ssl/ops-cockpit/cert.pem`\n  - `/etc/ssl/ops-cockpit/key.pem`\n  - service running in TLS mode.\n- [x] Added NAT redirect workaround for access without custom port:\n  - iptables redirects `443 -> 18888`.\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Stabilize external access UX and remove certificate warnings by moving from self-signed cert to trusted CA (Let’s Encrypt + domain).\n- [ ] Further refine Vietnamese natural-language quality for some legacy mixed log lines.\n\n### Blocked\n- Browser trust issue due self-signed certificate (`NET::ERR_CERT_AUTHORITY_INVALID`).\n- Some client networks appear to block direct custom port `18888` (`ERR_TIMED_OUT`), mitigated by 443 redirect.\n- No domain provided yet for trusted TLS issuance.\n- iptables redirect persistence across reboot not yet finalized.\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Custom lightweight Python dashboard**: Chosen for rapid delivery of realtime monitoring + custom AI workflow features.\n- **Basic Auth + systemd**: Added quickly for immediate controlled access and process resilience.\n- **Self-signed HTTPS first**: Used to unlock secure-context features (voice/camera) before domain/CA setup.\n- **443 NAT redirect to 18888**: Implemented to bypass custom-port reachability issues and simplify URL.\n- **Vietnamese-first + hide technicals by default**: Implemented per user preference with expandable technical context.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Confirm current access path with user: `https://103.173.66.241` (no port), accept initial cert warning if prompted.\n2. Ask user for domain, then migrate to trusted TLS (Let’s Encrypt) on 443 to remove browser warning.\n3. Persist network rules cleanly (or replace NAT workaround with proper reverse proxy on 443).\n4. Rotate dashboard credentials after stabilization (password currently exposed in chat context).\n5. Add media governance hardening (upload size limits, retention/cleanup policy).\n6. Continue Vietnamese phrasing cleanup for residual mixed-language technical details.\n\n## Critical Context\n- Main app files:\n  - `/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/ops_cockpit/server.py`\n  - `/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/ops_cockpit/public/index.html`\n- Service:\n  - `/etc/systemd/system/ops-cockpit.service` (HTTPS profile)\n  - `systemctl status ops-cockpit.service` was active/running.\n- Auth/TLS:\n  - `/etc/default/ops-cockpit` (contains `OPS_COCKPIT_PASS=...`)\n  - `/etc/ssl/ops-cockpit/cert.pem`\n  - `/etc/ssl/ops-cockpit/key.pem`\n- Important endpoints:\n  - `GET /api/metrics`\n  - `POST /api/minh-chat`\n  - `POST /api/upload-image`\n  - `GET /api/chat-history`\n  - `GET /uploads/<file>`\n- Access behavior observed:\n  - `https://103.173.66.241:18888` caused timeout for user in screenshot.\n  - NAT workaround added for `https://103.173.66.241` via 443 redirect.\n- Notable exact errors encountered:\n  - `NET::ERR_CERT_AUTHORITY_INVALID`\n  - `ERR_TIMED_OUT`\n  - `HTTP/1.0 501 Unsupported method ('HEAD')` (server doesn’t implement HEAD)\n  - `sudo: a password is required` (before sudo permissions update)\n  - `gateway closed (1008): pairing required` (subagent weather attempt).\n- Team-log and memory files updated heavily:\n  - `/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/team_logs/2026-04-13.md`\n  - `/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-04-13.md` (durable memory appended).\n\n---\n\n**Turn Context (split turn):**\n\n## Original Request\n- User asked to **change reporting cadence** to only send at **17:00** (instead of every hour).\n- User also asked why **RAM usage is high**.\n- User checked whether the assistant can see messages and asked why there was no interaction.\n\n## Early Progress\n- Assistant started by reading team logs (`2026-04-13.md` and `2026-04-12.md`) to recover context before responding.\n- From `2026-04-13` log, key prior decisions/context found:\n  - Assistant identity established as **MINH AI (Scrum PM)**, coordinating team members.\n  - Team roster had been reported as 4 core members.\n  - A Sprint 1 CRM MVP plan had been drafted earlier.\n  - A prior request had set up/expected **hourly reporting** (Vietnam time structure).\n  - Progress confidence was limited due to missing/evidence-light updates from owners.\n- `2026-04-12` log appeared essentially empty (no substantive entries).\n\n## Context for Suffix\n- The immediate issue in this turn is operational: user wants to **override hourly reports with a single 17:00 report**.\n- There is also a system concern to address: **high RAM consumption**.\n- User felt ignored, so responsiveness/acknowledgment is important in the follow-up.\n- Existing logs indicate prior automation/reporting expectations were in place, so suffix likely needs to update that schedule and explain system behavior.\n\n<read-files>\n/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/HEARTBEAT.md\n/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/team_logs/2026-04-12.md\n~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/weather/SKILL.md\n</read-files>\n\n<modified-files>\n/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-04-13.md\n/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/ops_cockpit/ops-cockpit-https.service\n/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/ops_cockpit/ops-cockpit.service\n/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/ops_cockpit/public/index.html\n/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/ops_cockpit/server.py\n/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/team_logs/2026-04-13.md\n</modified-files>","firstKeptEntryId":"5d05aa85","tokensBefore":232106,"details":{"readFiles":["/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/HEARTBEAT.md","/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/team_logs/2026-04-12.md","~/.npm-global/lib/node_modules/openclaw/skills/weather/SKILL.md"],"modifiedFiles":["/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-04-13.md","/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/ops_cockpit/ops-cockpit-https.service","/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/ops_cockpit/ops-cockpit.service","/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/ops_cockpit/public/index.html","/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/ops_cockpit/server.py","/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/team_logs/2026-04-13.md"]},"fromHook":false}
