OST `/api/upload-image` returns file URL; HTTPS POST `/api/minh-chat` with attachment returns polite Vietnamese acknowledgement and history payload. RAG: GREEN (channel capability delivered), AMBER for production-grade media governance (retention policy/size limits not yet enforced). Owners: Huy AI (chat+media UI), Hà AI (chat/upload APIs), Mạnh AI (deploy/restart HTTPS), PM validation MINH AI. ETA: done now. Blockers: no media retention/cleanup policy yet; camera permission depends on browser user consent. Next: add file-size limit + retention cleanup + optional image moderation/log policy.\n- 08:12–08:13 UTC: User reported web inaccessible after HTTPS migration. Verification evidence: service healthy (`ops-cockpit.service` active), port 18888 listening, local HTTPS responds (HTTP 200 with auth). Likely user-side access issue due protocol/cert flow (must use https + accept self-signed warning) or network path on custom port. Decision: provide immediate recovery instructions and propose mitigation path (move to trusted cert + standard 443). RAG: AMBER (service up, access friction exists). Owners: Mạnh AI investigate connectivity path, Huy AI provide user guidance UX banner, PM coordinate comms. ETA: immediate guidance now; 30–60m for 443/trusted-cert plan after user approval. Blockers: self-signed cert warning + possible custom-port reachability constraints. Next: confirm user can open explicit HTTPS URL; if still fail, execute migration to domain/443.\n- 08:12 UTC: User sent screenshot evidence showing browser warning `NET::ERR_CERT_AUTHORITY_INVALID` on `https://103.173.66.241:18888`. Decision: classify issue as expected self-signed certificate trust warning (not service outage). Immediate mitigation: instruct user to proceed via Advanced/Continue for temporary access; strategic mitigation: migrate to trusted CA certificate on domain (Let’s Encrypt) and optionally standard 443. RAG: AMBER (access possible with bypass, UX not production-grade). Owners: Mạnh AI (trusted cert path), Huy AI (onscreen guidance text), PM (decision support). ETA: guidance immediate; trusted-cert rollout after domain confirmation. Blockers: no domain-bound trusted cert yet.\n- 08:17–08:20 UTC: User sent new screenshot showing `ERR_TIMED_OUT` to `https://103.173.66.241:18888`. Investigation evidence: service is healthy and listening; likely network path blocks custom port 18888 from client side. Mitigation implemented immediately: added host-level NAT redirect 443 -> 18888 so dashboard is reachable via standard HTTPS endpoint without custom port; validated successful authenticated GET on `https://103.173.66.241/` (HTTP 200). RAG: GREEN for availability recovery path; AMBER for certificate trust warning (self-signed) still present. Owners: Mạnh AI (network redirect), Hà AI (service validation), PM (user comms). ETA: done now. Blockers: browser still warns until trusted CA/domain is configured. Next: instruct user to open `https://103.173.66.241` (no port) and continue via Advanced once.\n- 08:00–08:02 UTC: Internal scrum sync executed via sessions_spawn with explicit agentId (manh/huy/ha/huyen) and evidence-based 4-field updates collected. Decision: giữ focus 1 giờ tới vào chuyển từ planning sang artifact thực thi (OpenAPI/event spec/ticket assignment/SIT unlock), không mở rộng scope mới. RAG: Overall AMBER (all owners responded with evidence, but implementation artifacts/tickets still missing). Owner updates & ETA: Mạnh AI—08:05–08:20 chốt OpenAPI v1, 08:20–08:40 event envelope + idempotency rule, 08:40–09:00 contract-test checklist; Huy AI—08:01–08:10 nhận ticket/branch/PR, 08:10–08:35 tổng hợp FE artifact, 08:35–08:50 lint/test quick check, 08:50–09:00 cập nhật log; Hà AI—08:05–08:15 nhận assignment + AC, 08:15–08:35 backend design v0 nếu có scope, 08:35–09:00 scaffold PoC endpoint hoặc escalate; Huyền AI—08:05–08:20 chốt owner+ETA cho gateway/UAT data, 08:20–08:40 checklist go/no-go SIT, 08:40–09:00 cập nhật risk log. Blockers: (1) thiếu ticket/PR