{"type":"compaction","id":"91f90cbb","parentId":"7b429854","timestamp":"2026-04-13T14:22:11.206Z","summary":"## Goal\n- Maintain and operate a Vietnamese-first **Ops Cockpit** dashboard for anh Minh with realtime system/project monitoring, blocker visibility, and direct chat/voice interaction.\n- Keep interaction quality high (responsive, polite, evidence-based) and reporting governance clear.\n- **Expanded goal:** collect annual financial report data for Vietnamese banks (per provided template), for **2024 and 2025** (not quarterly), then fill template accurately.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Address user as **“anh Minh”/“sếp”**, respectful Vietnamese tone.\n- UI/reports should be **Vietnamese-first**; technical details hidden by default with expandable controls.\n- Reporting governance:\n  - Official periodic report: **1 lần lúc 17:00 giờ VN**, not hourly.\n  - Include explicit **blocker** section (RAG, owner, ETA, mitigation).\n- During current financial-data task, user requested very frequent progress pings:\n  - changed from 10 phút/lần to **2 phút/lần**, and timestamps in **ICT (UTC+7)**.\n- Accuracy over cost: user explicitly said prioritize correctness; token usage is not a constraint.\n- Financial collection scope finalized:\n  - **Annual reports** (not quarterly),\n  - banks strictly from template list,\n  - if captcha: mark **PENDING** and notify user.\n- `openpyxl` installation allowed.\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Previously completed platform work preserved: dashboard service/systemd/auth/TLS-self-signed, realtime metrics, blocker module, voice mode, image upload, camera capture, Vietnamese UX refinements, etc.\n- [x] Reporting cadence changed from hourly to **17:00 VN only** (official report), repeatedly reconfirmed.\n- [x] RAM diagnostics and optimization completed:\n  - Identified heavy processes (`openclaw-gateway`, `node` extension host, stale `openclaw/openclaw-tui`).\n  - Removed stale processes and reclaimed memory (roughly from ~2.6Gi used to ~1.1Gi used at best point).\n- [x] Chat session/history architecture implemented:\n  - Backend added persistent multi-session support (`CHAT_SESSIONS_FILE`), `GET/POST /api/chat-sessions`, `GET /api/chat-history?sessionId=...`.\n  - `/api/minh-chat` updated to accept `sessionId` and return per-session history.\n- [x] Frontend chat UX enhanced:\n  - session selector, create new session, load history.\n  - error-handling `try/catch` added for silent fetch failures.\n- [x] Weather intent bug fixed in chat:\n  - Added `_fetch_weather_summary_vi()` and weather intent handling in `generate_minh_reply`.\n- [x] Model governance clarified and locked:\n  - Current runtime for all bots remains `github-copilot/gpt-5.3-codex`.\n  - User decided to keep highest available in GitHub Student context; no A/B rollout now.\n- [x] Document upload feature added to chat:\n  - Backend `POST /api/upload-document` + `save_base64_file(...)` with mime/size checks.\n  - Frontend added “Gửi tài liệu” and `docPicker`.\n- [x] Bot-conversation feed improved:\n  - Added `recent_internal_agent_messages(...)` and merged into `build_chat_messages(...)` so `projects.chat` can reflect actual internal assistant messages.\n- [x] Financial task bootstrap completed:\n  - Installed `python3-pip` and `openpyxl`.\n  - Parsed template structure (2 sheets) and extracted **30-bank** list.\n  - Created working dir: `/home/openclaw_user/.openclaw/workspace/financial_reports_annual_2024_2025`.\n  - Pulled first artifacts (Techcombank PDFs):  \n    `bao-cao-thuong-nien-nam-2024-vie.pdf`, `fy25-press-release-vie.pdf`.\n- [x] HEARTBEAT instructions followed when triggered (`HEARTBEAT_OK` responses).\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Scale annual-report crawling from initial artifacts to all 30 banks and fill template columns for 2024/2025.\n- [ ] Improve crawler strategy for JS-heavy IR sites (especially VPB) and normalize source extraction.\n- [ ] Convert downloaded reports into mapped template values with QA checks.\n- [ ] Improve dashboard visibility for “bot assigned tasks / bot-to-bot coordination” (user still reports poor visibility).\n- [ ] Trusted TLS migration (domain + Let’s Encrypt) still pending.\n\n### Blocked\n- JS-rendered/hidden IR link structures (notably VPB) make static `curl` extraction unreliable.\n- No robust headless/browser automation pipeline yet for all banks.\n- Self-signed cert still causes browser trust warning.\n- Frequent manual progress cadence (2-minute reporting) is operationally brittle without automated push loop.\n- Conversation ended with assistant timeout before responding to queued user message.\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **17:00 VN official reporting only**: hourly cron-style report cadence is stopped.\n- **Blocker-first reporting format**: each report must include blocker severity, owner, ETA, mitigation.\n- **Accuracy-first mode for financial task**: prioritize correct numbers and verification over token/cost savings.\n- **Financial scope finalized**: annual reports for **2024 + 2025**, banks from template only, captcha => **PENDING**.\n- **Model configuration kept unchanged**: all bots stay on `github-copilot/gpt-5.3-codex` for now.\n- **Chat web is primary operational channel** (Telegram-like usage expected).\n- **Quick-win crawl approach**: prioritized VPB/TCB first; TCB yielded initial downloadable artifacts.\n- **Progress cadence altered by user**: 10-minute then 2-minute pings, with **ICT timestamps**.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Implement/enable stronger crawler method (headless or endpoint-discovery workflow) for JS-heavy bank IR pages.\n2. Continue collecting annual-report files bank-by-bank; maintain `DONE/PENDING` ledger with source URLs and captcha flags.\n3. Parse current TCB artifacts into template fields and produce first validated populated output slice.\n4. Add explicit “task assigned / bot status / inter-bot exchange” panel behavior so user can see coordination state clearly.\n5. Maintain progress updates in ICT format as requeste